{
  "id": "ledger-op-context-typed",
  "origin": "regression",
  "ledger_item": "ledger:rig-grade-swarm/phases/p139",
  "behaviour": "Every function of a module the ledger core dispatches an op to by name takes the op context as the one Protocol, OpContext, which holds what an op reads and writes of one sync: at, rev, events, refused, dropped, unstored, meta, slug, dirty and stamps, and the calls author, record and stamp. A ctx left untyped, or typed Any, object or the concrete class, is refused, in a function and in a method alike, and so is a dispatched module in which no function takes the context. The dispatched modules are discovered by where they live, never by their name and never hand kept: every module a registry dict of the core holds, and every module inside the ledger package folder that the core's own source hands the context to, resolved from any import shape (a plain import, an aliased import, a from-import of a submodule or of a function, module level or inside a function), plus the core itself. A function of the core that rebinds its context to another name before handing it on is refused too. The one concrete context, ledger_core.Context, holds every member of the Protocol. A live check prints one line per discovered module of the installed build, then one line per rebinding, and fails on the first of these that does not hold. The Semgrep rule grades every scripts/swarm_ledger/ledger_*.py file by one glob, with no hand kept list of its own, and that glob is proven to cover every module the live check discovers.",
  "seam": "scripts.swarm_ledger.op_context.OpContext against every function with a ctx parameter in the modules scripts.feature_checks.op_context_typed.op_modules discovers from scripts.swarm_ledger.ledger_core: its registry dicts and every module inside the ledger package folder its own source hands the op context to, located by import and call shape rather than by name",
  "semgrep_rule": "feature-ledger-op-context-typed",
  "live_check": [
    "python",
